# Address books are GENERATED by script/DeployTestnet.s.sol, one per deployment.
#
# They are ignored by default on purpose. `test/script/DeployTestnet.t.sol` runs the real script
# in-process, which writes a real-looking `46630.json` full of in-memory test addresses. Committed,
# that file would be indistinguishable from a genuine deployment record and a front-end reading it
# would point at contracts that exist on no chain.
#
# TO RECORD A GENUINE DEPLOYMENT: `git add -f deployments/<chainId>.json`, and check the `commit`
# field is a real commit hash (set `COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD)` when running the script) before
# you do. NEVER HAND-EDIT one: each mirror is a new vault AND a new certificate token, so an edited
# map silently repoints a UI at a new token while real balances sit in the old one. Re-run the
# script instead.
*.json

# EXCEPT mainnet (chain 4663). No test writes a 4663 book: the only suite that switches to chain
# 4663 (CommitGuard) calls the commit guard and never runs the script. An IGNORED new mainnet
# book, by contrast, is how live deployments went unrecorded: 4663.json was deleted and not
# noticed (ROADMAP 6.22), and three history books sat untracked while the README described them.
# A new mainnet book must show up in `git status`, not wait for someone to remember `-f`.
!4663.json
!4663.*.json
!history/
!history/4663.*.json
